Large positive responses mark auxiliaries immediately after 'why', or the
number in 'no one/two', 'any two', and 'only two'. Weaker responses cover
other question heads, small-number determiner phrases, reciprocal and
partitive phrases, and indefinite 'new'. Small baselines cover modal verbs
and quantity words; most other lexical variation is left at zero.
Only two preceding token spellings are kept; documents reset this memory.
