"""A spelling-based approximation of a negative h/digraph response.

Initial ch, sh, ph, sch, and less-common th spellings receive negative
values. Common grammatical words and listed word families are weaker;
shall and therm- are strong cases. Length, capitalization, word spacing,
and inflection adjust the main digraph response. Similar hushing letters
in Cyrillic, Arabic, and Japanese get coarse negative estimates.
Single underscores and tab-plus-space indentation are secondary cases.
Only the current token is used; context-dependent and lexical variation
within these groups is not reconstructed.
"""

READS = ()

FUNCTION_WORDS = frozenset("""
the they their theirs them themselves that than this these those then there
therefore thus though through throughout thereto thereof thereby thereafter
herein here how he her hers herself him himself his has have had having
however hence should shouldn she
