'Its' is strongest, followed by 'it'/'itself' and possessive determiners.
Capitalization, word boundaries and context starts change their strength.
The preceding word helps distinguish possessive apostrophe-s from contractions.
It also adjusts 'it' after clause-opening words versus verbs. Selected Russian,
German, Romance and Chinese reference or possessive forms are recognized too.
Other tokens usually receive zero: their small, irregular activations are omitted.
